 "cross_map_definition": "ridge fitted DIRECTLY from X = v_context(source) to Y = v_answer(target), scored on the target's held-out answers; NOT a tier and NOT bounded by the ceiling",
 "ci_note": "tier R2 intervals are the 1,000-draw paired-bootstrap GAP CI mapped through r2 = within_r2 - gap. Round-B pairs (SFT->RLVR, SFT->longer, RLVR->longer) carry no bootstrap draws and are point-only; no interval is borrowed. The cross map is point-only on every pair.",
